1
00:00:02,267 --> 00:00:03,537
(Howard:)It's pretty late.

2
00:00:03,535 --> 00:00:05,735
(Howard:)You think I've got time
to run some more simulations

3
00:00:05,737 --> 00:00:06,937
(Howard:)on the cooling system?

4
00:00:06,938 --> 00:00:08,208
(Leonard:)Sure, I'm still figuring out

5
00:00:08,206 --> 00:00:09,406
(Leonard:)the thermo-acoustic expander.

6
00:00:09,407 --> 00:00:10,507
(Sheldon:)Oh, while you do that

7
00:00:10,508 --> 00:00:13,848
(Sheldon:)I am going to pump
cerebral spinal fluid

8
00:00:13,845 --> 00:00:17,045
(Sheldon:)through my brain cells to remove
the metabolic by-products

9
00:00:17,048 --> 00:00:18,918
(Sheldon:)of the day's thoughts.

10
00:00:18,917 --> 00:00:20,947
(Howard:)What?

11
00:00:20,952 --> 00:00:22,522
(Sheldon:)It's called sleep
and it's my bedtime.

12
00:00:22,520 --> 00:00:24,320
(Sheldon:)Nighty-night, y'all.

13
00:00:24,322 --> 00:00:26,622
(Howard:)Hey, hey, hey,
you're not going anywhere.

14
00:00:26,625 --> 00:00:28,855
(Leonard:)We only have two months to
deliver this to the Air Force

15
00:00:28,860 --> 00:00:29,890
(Leonard:)because of you.

16
00:00:29,895 --> 00:00:32,665
(Sheldon:)I know, I was there.

17
00:00:32,664 --> 00:00:34,164
Well, wake up!

18
00:00:34,165 --> 00:00:36,265
(Howard:)We're gonna put in
a lot of late nights.

19
00:00:36,268 --> 00:00:37,598
(Sheldon:)How late?

20
00:00:37,602 --> 00:00:40,842
(Howard:)Well, I don't know,
midnight, 1:00.

21
00:00:40,839 --> 00:00:41,839
(Sheldon:)One o'clock?

22
00:00:41,840 --> 00:00:44,110
(Sheldon:)I'm not a raccoon.

23
00:00:44,109 --> 00:00:47,279
(Howard:)If you're tired,
have some coffee.

24
00:00:47,279 --> 00:00:48,749
(Howard:)What?
You have some coffee.

25
00:00:48,747 --> 00:00:50,447
I am having coffee!

26
00:00:50,448 --> 00:00:52,178
(Sheldon:)And look how irritable
it's making you!

27
00:00:52,183 --> 00:00:54,213
Guys!

28
00:00:54,219 --> 00:00:56,089
(Leonard:)We're not gonna get anything
done if we start fighting.

29
00:00:56,087 --> 00:00:58,257
(Leonard:)Now, can you please try
to soldier through?

30
00:00:59,424 --> 00:01:00,954
(Sheldon:)Fine.

31
00:01:14,906 --> 00:01:17,836
(Sheldon:)I don't think
I can go much longer.

32
00:01:17,842 --> 00:01:19,912
(Leonard:)It's been three and a half
minutes, wake up!

33
00:01:21,413 --> 00:01:25,053
♪ Our whole universe
was in a hot, dense state ♪

